{
  "slug": "tylor",
  "name": "Tylor",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "▎ Eliminates Claude session death. Gives Claude persistent named threads — isolated\n  ▎  context scopes that survive restarts, machine changes, and version updates.     \n  ▎ Switch between projects instantly with zero re-priming. Includes silent code     \n  ▎ indexing (Claude navigates directly to the right file/line), a live thread     \n  ▎ visualizer, agent personas (CEO, CTO, Analyst, Code Agent), and AFK autonomous\n  ▎ execution.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **11 skills** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (11): `add-skill` (Install an agent101 skill package by copying it into skills/ and generating a registry.json entry), `afk-status` (Report current AFK execution progress for the active thread), `bmad` (Use when the user wants to create a PRD, review stories, or run BMAD workflows), `help-agent101` (Show a current structured listing of agent101 commands, tools, skills, personas, and ECC categories), `kill-thread` (Close an agent101 thread with kill_thread and confirm that async summarization has started), `list-threads` (List agent101 threads by calling list_threads and formatting active, killed, and message_count details), `new-thread` (Create a new agent101 thread by prompting for a thread name and calling the new_thread MCP tool), `recall` (Recall relevant agent101 memory facts by asking for a thread ID and query, then calling recall_memory), and 3 more\n- **MCP servers** (1): `agent101`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install tylor@claude-community` from `GunjanGrunge/tylor`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 11,
    "mcp": 1
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
